# What must NOT go into the frontend image's build context.
#
# A second file rather than one at the repository root, because Docker reads the `.dockerignore`
# at the root of the BUILD CONTEXT — and `docker build ./frontend` makes that this directory. The
# root file covers `docker build -f app/Dockerfile .`; it does nothing here.
#
# It matters more here than there, because `frontend/Dockerfile` does `COPY . .`: without this,
# a local `node_modules/` is shipped to the daemon and copied into the image, where `npm ci` has
# just installed the exact tree the lockfile specifies. That is the reproducibility the Dockerfile's
# own comment argues for, undone by whatever happens to be lying around.

node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/

# Test and demo artefacts — the recordings alone run to megabytes.
test-results/
playwright-report/
.playwright/
demo-recordings/

# Local environment and editors
.env
.env.local
.DS_Store
